pageType: content
background:
  type: solid
  color: "$bg"
elements:
  - elementId: kicker
    elementType: text
    bounds: [80, 48, 500, 20]
    content:
      style: "$kicker"
      wrap: false
      text: "06 — USE CASE COVERAGE: THREE DEMOS, FIVE MINUTES"
  - elementId: d1-title
    elementType: text
    bounds: [80, 92, 470, 26]
    content:
      fontSize: 18
      bold: true
      color: "$text"
      wrap: false
      text: "Catch a missing API requirement"
  - elementId: d1-body
    elementType: text
    bounds: [80, 122, 470, 74]
    content:
      style: "$body"
      text: |
        <p>The story says nothing about auth, errors or headers. Compass finds the project standard (standards/api-standard.md:10) and asks. Checks then flag the spec — no X-Correlation-Id, no 400 on POST, no auth. <span style="color:$warn"><strong>Verdict: Not accepted yet.</strong></span></p>
  - elementId: d-sep1
    elementType: line
    bounds: [80, 204, 470, 2]
    viewBox: [470, 2]
    points: "0,1 470,1"
    border: {style: solid, width: 1, color: "$line"}
  - elementId: d2-title
    elementType: text
    bounds: [80, 218, 470, 26]
    content:
      fontSize: 18
      bold: true
      color: "$text"
      wrap: false
      text: "Reject a fix without reproduction evidence"
  - elementId: d2-body
    elementType: text
    bounds: [80, 248, 470, 74]
    content:
      style: "$body"
      text: |
        <p>Tests run on temporary copies; your files are never changed. A fix with no failing-then-passing regression test is rejected. The fix with that test is <span style="color:$primary"><strong>accepted with evidence</strong></span> — reproducible, reviewable, honest.</p>
  - elementId: d-sep2
    elementType: line
    bounds: [80, 330, 470, 2]
    viewBox: [470, 2]
    points: "0,1 470,1"
    border: {style: solid, width: 1, color: "$line"}
  - elementId: d3-title
    elementType: text
    bounds: [80, 344, 470, 26]
    content:
      fontSize: 18
      bold: true
      color: "$text"
      wrap: false
      text: "A test that catches a seeded defect"
  - elementId: d3-body
    elementType: text
    bounds: [80, 374, 470, 74]
    content:
      style: "$body"
      text: |
        <p>A generated test detects the planted defect at auth.py:35. Smoke tests that pass on broken code are flagged as weak, with security candidates reported — a synthetic credential and shell=True.</p>
  - elementId: shot
    elementType: image
    bounds: [600, 110, 300, 275]
    src: "media/api-6-evidence.png"
    fit: {mode: cover}
    border: {style: solid, width: 1, color: "$line"}
  - elementId: shot-cap
    elementType: text
    bounds: [600, 396, 300, 36]
    content:
      style: "$small"
      text: |
        <p>Evidence step in the workflow coach — checks with imported results and file:line citations.</p>
  - elementId: pageno
    elementType: text
    bounds: [900, 500, 36, 16]
    content:
      style: "$small"
      align: [right, middle]
      wrap: false
      text: "08"
